--- Coverage for the `~` logic prefix, methods as rvalues, and method checks.

@let
  count int = 1
  other int = 7
  label string
  flag bool = true
  ratio float
@end

# start

Mutations with literal rvalues.

~ count = 5
~ count += 2
~ count -= 1
~ label = "hello"
~ ratio = 1.5
~ flag =!

Mutations with variable and method rvalues.

~ count = other
~ count += other
~ count = returns_something()
~ count += returns_something()
~ count -= returns_something()
~ label = returns_w_args(count, "x")

Whitespace is optional after the prefix.

~count = 3
~count+=1
~simple()
~   simple()

Method operations.

~ simple()
~ simple_args(5, "bob")
~ simple_args(count, label)
~ simple() --- end comment on a method
~ count = returns_something() --- end comment on a mutation

Inline conditionals.

(? returns_something()) Method check.
(? !returns_something()) Negated method check.
(? returns_something() and flag) Method and variable.
(? flag or returns_something()) Variable or method.
(? returns_something() > 3) Method compare.
(? count = returns_something()) Variable compare to method.
(? returns_w_args(count, "x") = "y") Method with args compare.
(? (returns_something() > 1) and !flag) Subclause with method.
(? returns_something()) ~ simple()
(? flag) ~ count = returns_something()

Injected {returns_something()} and {returns_w_args(1, "a")}.

> (? returns_something()) Conditional choice
  ~ simple()
  ~ count = returns_something()
> Plain choice
  ~count+=1

@if returns_something()

If on method.

@elseif returns_w_args(count, "z") = "z"

Elseif on method with args.

@elseif !returns_something() and flag

Elseif negated method and variable.

@else

Else.

@endif

EXIT
